  "shortDescription": "A sliding item carousel with looping and smooth tween transitions, driven by a single object.",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": [
    "Turns 2D sprite into a looping, sliding item carousel. Call **Next** or **Previous** to move between items, with a smooth slide-out/slide-in animation handled automatically.",
    "",
    "The item shown always matches the current animation index: index 0 is the object's first animation, index 1 the second, and so on.",
    "",
    "Use cases:",
    "- A level select screen, cycling through level previews",
    "- A character or skin picker",
    "- Any settings screen with a small set of choices to cycle through (difficulty, region, theme...)",
    "",
    "Setup:",
    "1. The Tween behavior is required and gets added automatically when you add Carousel.",
    "2. Set `MinIndex` and `MaxIndex` to match the number of animations on your object (0-based).",
    "3. Call `Next` / `Previous` from your arrow buttons, and read `CurrentIndex` to update the rest of your UI."
  ],
  "tags": [
